# Feature Migration: Real Image Loading in ScrollBench

## Goal
Replace the synthetic "colored rectangle" data in [ScrollBench](file:///d:/Dev/antigravity/test_scrollbench/src/ScrollBenchImageModel.cpp#7-9) with real image loading from the filesystem, reusing the main application's [AsyncImageProvider](file:///d:/Dev/antigravity/src/AsyncImageProvider.h#34-58). This will validate the performance optimizations against real-workloads.

## User Review Required
> [!IMPORTANT]
> This change will make ScrollBench require a valid image directory to function meaningfully, similar to the main app.

## Proposed Changes

### Core Logic
#### [MODIFY] [test_scrollbench/src/ScrollBenchImageModel.cpp](file:///d:/Dev/antigravity/test_scrollbench/src/ScrollBenchImageModel.cpp)
- **Remove** synthetic data generation (random colors).
- **Add** `folderPath` property to the model.
- **Implement** [scanDirectory()](file:///d:/Dev/antigravity/test_scrollbench/src/ScrollBenchImageModel.cpp#123-157) using `QDirIterator` (similar to [ImageModel](file:///d:/Dev/antigravity/test_scrollbench/src/ScrollBenchImageModel.cpp#7-9) in main app) to populate the model with real file paths.
- **Integrate** [AsyncImageProvider](file:///d:/Dev/antigravity/src/AsyncImageProvider.h#34-58):
    - Request thumbnails for visible items.
    - Handle `loaded` signals to update the model.

#### [MODIFY] [test_scrollbench/src/main_scrollbench.cpp](file:///d:/Dev/antigravity/test_scrollbench/src/main_scrollbench.cpp)
- Register [AsyncImageProvider](file:///d:/Dev/antigravity/src/AsyncImageProvider.h#34-58) as an image provider engine for QML (if not already done).

### UI
#### [MODIFY] [test_scrollbench/qml/MainScrollBench.qml](file:///d:/Dev/antigravity/test_scrollbench/qml/MainScrollBench.qml)
- Add a mechanism to set the folder path (hardcoded for test or a simple text field).
- Update delegates to show the `image://` provider URL instead of a rectangle color.

## Verification Plan
### Manual Verification
1. Run `appScrollBench.exe`.
2. Point it to a folder with thousands of images.
3. Verify images load.
4. Verify "Frame Budget" and "Viewport Culling" still function with real async workloads.
